on":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproduceable In: v4.5.stable.steam [876b29033]\n- Not Reproduceable In: v4.4 Stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26100) - Vulkan (Forward+) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7700) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 32 GB RAM\n\n### Issue description\n\nI went to go test something involving controller vibration earlier today in Godot 4.5 and noticed something peculiar, and upon testing realized that the strong and weak motor values have been SWAPPED on the Input.start_joy_vibration() function. I further tested outside of Godot and confirmed my controller is receiving the correct strong and weak values from other programs, not to mention the exact same code in Godot 4.4 works perfectly fine. Since the documentation both internal and external does not indicate a change in how this function works this _must_ be a bug.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Call Input.start_joy_vibration() in a script and feed it a value of 1.0 for the strong motor and the weak motor spins when run. Feed a value of 1.0 for the weak motor and the strong motor spins when run.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"http